msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md
msgid "a `github.com/<owner>/<repo>/blob/<ref>/<path>` URL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md
msgid ""
"rewritten to `raw.githubusercontent.com/<owner>/<repo>/<ref>/<path>`, "
"because fetching the `blob` page would hash a web page rather than a "
"document, and would do it silently. Both spellings are correct input"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md
msgid "`http://`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md
msgid ""
"accepted, and warned about once per run: the hash is what compensates for"
" an unauthenticated fetch, but you should know which kind you are doing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md
msgid "a bare relative path"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md
msgid ""
"accepted. In a **configuration file** it is resolved against the file's "
"own directory, because that file is searched for and one line in it is "
"read from many working directories; on the command line and in the "
"environment it is relative to the shell you typed it in"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md:76
msgid ""
"Sphinx publishes reStructuredText sources under `_sources/` with a `.txt`"
" suffix appended, which is why the default pattern ends in `.rst.txt` "
"rather than `.rst`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md:79
msgid "Fetching, the cache, and being offline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md:81
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Pages are fetched with `curl -fsSL` and cached, content-addressed, under "
"`${XDG_CACHE_HOME:-$HOME/.cache}/freeports-validate/<sha256 of the "
"URI>/<sha256 of the body>`. Every distinct body ever seen for a URI is "
"kept, and a `latest` symlink names the most recent one."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/reference/cli/methodology-sources.md:85
msgid ""
"**Online, the cache is a fallback and never a shortcut.** A run with a "
"network always fetches. A cache consulted first would quietly pin a "
"methodology to whatever was fetched the day you first saw it — and the "
"published text changing is precisely the event this whole mechanism "
"exists to notice."
msgstr ""

